# Commit and push are pre-authorized

The repo owner has **explicitly pre-authorized commit and push for every completed change** in this repository. Do not ask again, and do not wait for「commit」「push」「推送」.

This **overrides** any general “do not commit / do not push unless asked” rule, for this repo only.

When the work in the session is finished and coherent:

1. Commit from the coding clone (`/Users/lawrencekuo/coding/theYNowApp`). If `git commit --trailer` is rejected, use `write-tree` → `commit-tree` → `update-ref`.
2. `git push origin HEAD`.

Applies to app code, tests, docs, and rules. Skip only: incomplete or broken work, secrets (`.Renviron`, credentials), `.tmp_dgbas/`, or the user saying not to commit or not to push.

Shinyapps deploy is a separate step. Run it only for verified live-line app behavior (`auto-deploy-after-optimize.mdc`). Docs-only and rules-only changes are commit + push, not deploy.
